00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.269
you know from such shows
as "E.R." and "Six Feet Under."

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.339
She stars in the Netflix remake
of "One Day at a Time."

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
The third season
begins streaming Friday.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.175 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:14.180
-None of those things are legal
for you 'cause you're 15.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's just a fun thing we do
once in a while.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:18.451 line:92%
Anyways, I get straight A's.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:21.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you won't for long
if you're a stoner.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm not a stoner.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.490 size:84% position:42% line:92%
We laugh at those guys.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.160
Besides, tons of successful
people have smoked weed --

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.396 line:92%
Barack Obama, Steve Jobs, Oprah.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:35.035
-Unemployed, dead, and Gayle
just said that to get ratings.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.904
-Please welcome to the show,
Justina Machado, everyone!

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.173 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:50.183 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi, Justina.
How are you?

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi! I'm good.
I'm good.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations
on season three.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, for people
who don't watch this show,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is both
a traditional sitcom,

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:04.631 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but it also --

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:07.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it tackles issues
that are very modern.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:12.005
You play a Cuban-American,
war veteran, single mom,

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:12.906 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
dealing with PTSD.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you --
Could you kind of not believe

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you first started
seeing the scripts

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:20.647
exactly how, you know, real
the material was gonna be?

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, because, of course,
the first thing

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
that drew me to it
is that Norman Lear

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
was making a remake,
and I'm like "Norman Lear?

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:30.290
Of course, I'd love to work with
Norman Lear and Rita Moreno."

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I hadn't even
read anything yet,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when I had
to go read for him,

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they gave me the script,
is when I discovered,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.430 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"Wow, this is amazing."

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is such
a layered monologue.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:40.400 size:88% position:44% line:92%
There's so much in here.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.969 size:84% position:42%
You know, so many times
as a Latina actress,

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.204 line:92%
you're put in boxes, you know?

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.173
It's either you're like
the oversexualized Latina

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.174 line:92%
or you're the asexual cop

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:51.678
or you're the suffering mother,
or you're all of these things,

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:55.281 size:78% position:39%
and it was this woman
who was just layered

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just fantastic
and had so much humanity.

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah.
It was incredible.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.189
-And here is Norman, right here.
-Yes.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.591 line:92%
-You wouldn't think he's the guy

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's gonna help
a Latina be multi-layered.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.628 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there he is.
[ Applause ]

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the best of all-time.
-He is.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.501
He has a lot of help
from our wonderful showrunners,

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.070 size:88% position:44%
Gloria Calderon Kellett
and Mike Royce, so, yes.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:17.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yes. Definitely.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.939
-And it was lovely to meet
Gloria backstage, as well.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
She came to support me!

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The first season
led up to a quinceañera.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:25.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had one.
-I did.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had a really
ghetto quinceañera.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:30.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, how so?
-Well, you know,

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:33.520
I'm from a working-class family
in the inner city of Chicago,

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we didn't have
a lot of money.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:36.856 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So, my mother was like,

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, you're not having
a quinceañera,"

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.260
and I thought, "Yes, I am
having a quinceañera."

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.863
And I went around, and I asked
every family member for money,

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
and even my cousin
made the dress for me.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:50.970
We rented this ghetto hall
on North Avenue in Chicago --

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:55.175
in Chicago, called Norvell,
and upstairs from the hall

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.977 size:88% position:44% line:92%
was a hotel for hookers.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:02:59.979 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
So while I was -- while
my guests are walking out,

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
the hookers were coming in.
-Wow!

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was like,
"Yeah! This is good."

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you could imagine how much
the teenagers loved it.

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:12.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here it is!
This is a beautiful photo.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Come on.
Look at this.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Look at that hair.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Look at those things.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my God.
Yeah, that isn't cute.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:21.634
-You recently posted this photo
of how you used to love Prince

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:26.239
and that you ended up kind of
just, like, becoming Prince.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:28.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's fantastic.
-I mean, look at that.

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:31.878
But the sad thing is, I was
trying to look like Madonna.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yes, yes.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You aimed for Madonna
and hit Prince?

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-I did. Oh, my God!

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's hilarious.
I did.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:42.222
-We met years ago because
we have a friend in common.

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:43.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've known him
a lot longer than I have.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
Horatio Sanz.
-Horatio Sanz.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You knew him
from Chicago, as well.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
I've known him since

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:51.297
I was 18 years old, and we call
him Roger in Chicago.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.800
-Yeah.
-So, I might go back and forth.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah.
Roger and I --

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:59.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
Horatio and I -- Sorry.
Horatio and I,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were in the same
theater company together,

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:04.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
and funnily enough,
we auditioned

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
